>>
endobj
689 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 430 0 R
/E (           Most retention problems do not happen because coaches stop caring. They happen because there is no structure telling coaches when to act, what to say, or who needs attention right now. The three fixes in this chapter are powerful on their own. But when they run together as a system, they create something different -- a member experience so intentional that cancellation becomes genuinely difficult.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
690 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 430 0 R
/E (Here is exactly how the Retention Engine runs from Day 1 through Week 12.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
691 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 430 0 R
/E (Day 1 -- Intro and Onboarding The moment a new member walks in, two things happen. First, you show them where they sit on the Milestone Map. They need to see their starting point and their next target immediately. Second, you confirm their current goal and assign them to a specific coach. Not the gym in general. A specific person who now owns their experience.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
692 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 430 0 R
/E (Week 1 -- The Welcome Message Within 48 hours of their first class, their assigned coach sends a personal text or voice note. Not a template. Something that references what actually happened in their session. This one touch costs 60 seconds and tells the member they are already being noticed as a person, not processed as a transaction.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
693 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 430 0 R
/E (Weeks 2 and 3 -- Milestone Tracking Goes Live The coach updates the milestone board and makes sure the new member knows their position on it. They should be able to walk into your box and see exactly where they stand and exactly what they are working toward. That visibility is what keeps motivation alive before the novelty wears off.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
694 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 430 0 R
/E (Week 4 -- The Month-1 Check-In A 5 to 10 minute conversation, in person or by phone. Ask how they are feeling. Ask what they want to improve. Ask what would make this feel like home. Log every answer. These notes become the foundation of every future conversation. A member whose goals are written down and referenced later does not feel like a customer. They feel like someone this gym actually cares about.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
