endobj
1016 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 446 0 R
/E (         When a member refers a friend, they are not just sending you a lead -- they are pre-selling them. That friend arrives already trusting you, already motivated, and already connected to at least one person inside your community. Their likelihood of completing the first month, making it past the 90-day mark, and becoming a long-term member is significantly higher than anyone who clicked an ad and filled out a form at 11pm on a Tuesday. You are not just saving the acquisition cost -- you are getting a better member.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
1017 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 446 0 R
/E (     And the compounding effect is what most owners miss entirely. A referred member who stays 18 months and then refers two people of their own is not a $2,450 member. They are a $7,350 member. The flywheel does not just spin -- it accelerates. Every retained member makes the next referral more likely. Every recognized member becomes a louder advocate. Every community event deepens the loyalty that keeps the whole system moving. This is not a marketing tactic. It is the actual business model of the most profitable CrossFit boxes in the country.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
