/T (         You went through three complete systems -- retention, revenue, and community -- and you now have a clearer picture of your box's revenue potential than most owners ever get. That alone puts you in the top 5% of CrossFit owners in terms of clarity.)
/E (         You went through three complete systems -- retention, revenue, and community -- and you now have a clearer picture of your box's revenue potential than most owners ever get. That alone puts you in the top 5% of CrossFit owners in terms of clarity.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1244 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 456 0 R
/T (But clarity without action is just expensive awareness. And this is the moment where the gap between the owners who break through and the ones who stay stuck gets decided.)
/E (But clarity without action is just expensive awareness. And this is the moment where the gap between the owners who break through and the ones who stay stuck gets decided.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1245 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 456 0 R
/E (          You did not open a CrossFit box to manage a payroll that stresses you out every month. You did not become a coach to spend your nights wondering if the numbers are going to work. You did not build a community of people who trust you with their health, their time, and their money -- to watch that community slowly shrink because you could not crack the revenue problem.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1246 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 456 0 R
/E (           But that is what happens to most owners. Not because they are bad coaches. Not because their programming is weak. Not because their members do not love them.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
1247 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 456 0 R
/E (            It happens because the passion that builds a CrossFit box is not the same thing as the systems that scale one.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
1248 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 456 0 R
/E (            The churn climbs quietly. Revenue is there but profit feels like something that happens to other gym owners. You are coaching more classes than you ever planned to be at this stage. You know the gym has more potential -- you feel it every time you walk in and see your members pushing harder than people who pay three times as much at a commercial gym ever do. The product is not the problem. The problem is a great product trapped inside a leaky business. And the owners who break out of that cycle are not the ones with the best coaches or the best location -- they are the ones who decide that systems are not optional anymore. That moment is right now. The playbook is in your hands.)
/Pg 50 0 R
/K [13]
>>
endobj
